# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-list-hosts-ignored — alfe --list-hosts is accepted and does nothing
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-alfe-list-hosts-ignored

* Symptom

Split out of =alfe-host-selection-gaps= (alfe 2.2.77). The shared parser
accepts =--list-hosts= and sets =list-hosts-p=, but =alfe.cli:run= has no
branch for it, so with no other action alfe opens its REPL (=alfe> =) instead
of printing the hosts as =clautolisp --list-hosts= does. =--help= does not
list the option, and the user manual says alfe accepts it and does nothing.

* Proposal

Print the hosts and exit 0, like =--list-encodings= / =--list-dialects=. The
shared =clautolisp.autolisp-cli:print-hosts= prints a line about the retired
spellings of two hosts; alfe, which dropped them, should not repeat it, so
either alfe prints its own three lines or the shared list loses that note
(clautolisp-visible). Then: =--help=, the man page, the manual's "Host
selection" (the "Two clautolisp options alfe does not have" paragraph), a
scenario.

* Acceptance criteria

- =alfe --list-hosts= prints cador, cadtui, nihil with a one-line summary
  each and exits 0, opening no REPL.
- Documented in =--help=, the man page and the user manual.
